Run: `nix develop .#testing -c tests/fixtures/families/load_run.sh mes1`. i(vd) in A, |i(vd)| at 1 GHz for acg/acd.
nom is 27 C, m=1, the control of off (80 C, m=3); both give area=2. The model has no temperature law on either side (off is nom times m to 1e-12). ngspice-45 lists no `m`
in the MESFET parameter table (devices/mes/mes.c) and still multiplies by it, as VACASK's $mfactor does.
The oracle of the AC readings (fd.py, last lines): nom_sat's operating point moved 1e-4 V on the gate and the drain,
whose central differences are gm and gds of the DC law, against |i(vd)| at 1 kHz.
Result: no difference. DC agrees in every region (4.2e-5 at most, a cutoff pA current), AC to 3e-13, and both
simulators' AC are their DC law's derivatives (fd.py: within the differences' own 1e-6).

